@dec21_honour_settlement
title: Honour the merger settlement and keep PPS as an internal current
subtitle: No mandates leave the common Left, and the PPS current gains a protected reason to remain.
view-if: pps_breakaway_pressure < 28
on-arrival: pps_active = 1; pps_in_left = 1; pps_party_formed = 0; pps_dissent -= 10; party_unity += 4; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The inclusive merger settlement survives its first enforcement test"

= The merger settlement survives first contact

The leadership enforces the earlier truce exactly as written, and the PPS
deputies keep their seats inside the common caucus. Nobody gets a triumphant
headline, but the practical effect is visible: one less splinter, one less
evening spent counting who has already left.

The compromise does not erase distrust. It does prove that a signed internal
settlement can still survive first contact with a real defection threat.

- @december_2021_hub: Return to the December desk

@dec21_amnesty
title: Offer an amnesty and a binding internal appeal
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The mediation has no organisational backing.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; party_unity += 5; labor_dissent -= 5; progressives_dissent -= 4; pps_dissent -= 12; pps_strength += 1; pps_active = 1; pps_in_left = 1; pps_party_formed = 0; barons_dissent += 4; merger_resolution = "Amnesty and internal appeal"; news_headline = "An amnesty gives the tiny PPS current a protected place"

= The amnesty buys procedure, not peace

Lewica spends scarce organisational capacity to buy time and procedure instead
of a purge. The appeal mechanism keeps the PPS current inside one chain of
command, but everyone now knows this peace is expensive and conditional.

Barons read the move as another concession to minority currents; labor and
progressive organisers read it as proof that exits are not the only language
the party still understands.

- @december_2021_hub: Return to the December desk

@dec21_accept
title: Accept the circle and negotiate parliamentary cooperation
on-arrival: {!
const ppsSeatTarget = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0), 3
);
let ppsSeats = Math.min(
    ppsSeatTarget,
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_pps_seats) || 0)
);
Q.left_pps_seats = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.left_pps_seats) || 0) - ppsSeats
);
for (const seatKey of [
    "left_barons_seats", "left_labor_seats",
    "left_progressives_seats", "left_spring_seats", "razem_seats"
]) {
    const transfer = Math.min(
        ppsSeatTarget - ppsSeats,
        Math.max(0, Number(Q[seatKey]) || 0)
    );
    Q[seatKey] = Math.max(0, (Number(Q[seatKey]) || 0) - transfer);
    ppsSeats += transfer;
}
const ppsSenators = Math.min(
    2,
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.senate_left_seats) || 0)
);
Q.party_unity -= 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.pps_circle_relation = 55;
Q.pps_party_relation = 55;
Q.pps_exit_strength = Math.max(1, Number(Q.pps_strength) || 2);
Q.pps_active = 0;
Q.pps_in_left = 0;
Q.pps_org_status = "departed";
Q.pps_party_formed = 1;
Q.pps_party_name = "PPS";
Q.pps_demand_answered = 1;
Q.pps_escalation_stage = 0;
Q.pps_last_crisis_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.rozenek_in_left = 0;
Q.morawska_stanecka_in_left = 0;
Q.pps_strength = 0;
Q.pps_dissent = 100;
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) - ppsSeats);
Q.pps_party_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.pps_party_seats) || 0) + ppsSeats;
Q.senate_left_seats = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.senate_left_seats) - ppsSenators
);
Q.senate_independent_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.senate_independent_seats) || 0) + ppsSenators;
Q.pps_senate_seats = ppsSenators;
Q.seat_subvention_seats = Q.left_seats;
Q.left_new_generation_seats =
    (Number(Q.left_labor_seats) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0);
Q.nowa_lewica_seats =
    (Number(Q.left_barons_seats) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.left_spring_seats) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.left_labor_seats) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0);
Q.barons_dissent -= 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The PPS circle leaves the common whip without becoming an enemy";
!}

= Cooperation survives, unity does not

The PPS circle leaves the common whip, but it exits through a negotiated lane
rather than a blood feud. Seat arithmetic worsens immediately, yet a working
channel remains open for selected parliamentary votes.

Inside Lewica, the compromise feels untidy and weak to hardliners. Outside it,
the split reads as manageable rather than terminal.

- @december_2021_hub: Return to the December desk

